    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-41" id="fn-41" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Intangible rate for line 9 is based on a 5-year depreciable basis.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-42" id="fn-42" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Enterprise shared service costs are allocated to franchises via specific or general methods. Specific allocations are based on metrics that bear a reasonable correlation to the delivery of services, for instance some human resource services costs are allocated based on employee headcount. General allocations are based on "Modified Massachusetts" formula (MMF) which is determined by the proportion of three components: net revenues; gross property, plant and equipment; and gross payroll.</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-43" id="fn-43" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Enterprise shared service costs for fleet leasing and other fleet costs are allocated to franchises via specific allocations based on labor costs assigned to capital work orders.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-44" id="fn-44" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Payroll and non-payroll charges for the benefit of the operating area that are not specific to a franchise are allocated to franchises in the operating area via specific or general methods. Specific allocations are based on metrics that bear a reasonable correlation to the delivery of services, for instance some human resource services costs are allocated based on employee headcount. General allocations are based on "Modified Massachusetts" formula (MMF) which is determined by the proportion of three components: net revenues; gross property, plant and equipment; and gross payroll.</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-45" id="fn-45" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Storage facilities charges recorded to a specific work order for the benefit of the storage facilities within Transmission, Power &amp; Gulf Operating Area that are not specific to a franchise are allocated to franchises included in the operating area via specific allocations primarily based on labor costs.</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-46" id="fn-46" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:19pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Employees' direct assignment payroll and non-payroll charges recorded to a specific work order for the benefit of the Transmission, Power &amp; Gulf Operating Area that are not specific to a franchise are allocated to franchises included in the operating area via general allocations based on "Modified Massachusetts" formula (MMF).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-47" id="fn-47" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Houston, Texas Williams tower building rent is allocated based on employee labor hours.</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-48" id="fn-48" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">Common systems hardware and software costs are allocated via general allocations using "Modified Massachusetts" formula (MMF).</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-49" id="fn-49" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <span xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">MountainWest shared services costs are allocated to MountainWest Pipeline, LLC, MountainWest Overthrust Pipeline, LLC, White River Hub, LLC, and nonregulated companies via specific allocations for pipeline companies based on miles of pipe and general allocations for the other companies based on "Modified Massachusetts" formula (MMF).</span>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-50" id="fn-50" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:19pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Salt Lake City, Utah building rent is allocated based on employee labor hours.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-51" id="fn-51" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:19pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Salt Lake City, Utah building rent is allocated based on employee labor hours.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-52" id="fn-52" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:19pt">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">MountainWest shared services costs are allocated to MountainWest Pipeline, LLC, MountainWest Overthrust Pipeline, LLC, White River Hub, LLC, and nonregulated companies via specific allocations for pipeline companies based on miles of pipe and general allocations for the other companies based on "Modified Massachusetts" formula (MMF).</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-53" id="fn-53" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
